.TH DOCKERSOURCE 1 "2026-05-22" "dockersource repo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dockersource \- Docker Compose files for homelab containers and a Portainer stack sync tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ~/dockersource/portainer-convert.py
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B bash ~/dockersource/
.IB service-name /install.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B dockersource
repo provides two things:
.PP
1. A collection of ready-to-use Docker Compose files for common homelab containers, each with an
.B install.sh
and (where required) a
.B .env.example
for secrets.
.PP
2.
.BR portainer-convert.py ,
a CLI tool to convert Compose files to Portainer-safe YAML, deploy stacks, pull stacks, and sync changes.
.SH SETUP
.SS portainer-convert.py requirements
.PP
.RS
pip install pyyaml requests
.RE
.SS Configure connection
.PP
.RS
python3 portainer-convert.py config \\
.br
  --url https://<portainer-host>:9443 \\
.br
  --token ptr_xxxxxxxxxxxx \\
.br
  --no-verify-ssl
.RE
.PP
Settings are saved to
.IR ~/.portainer-convert.json .
All flags can also be passed per-command or via environment variables.
.SS Connection options
.TP
.B --portainer-url
Portainer base URL (env:
.BR PORTAINER_URL )
.TP
.B --token
API key starting with
.B ptr_
(env:
.BR PORTAINER_TOKEN )
.TP
.B --endpoint-id
Endpoint ID, default 1 (env:
.BR PORTAINER_ENDPOINT_ID )
.TP
.B --no-verify-ssl
Skip SSL verification (useful for self-signed certs)
.SH PORTAINER CONVERT TOOL
.TP
.B list
List all stacks in Portainer.
.RS
.PP
python3 portainer-convert.py list
.RE
.TP
.B to-portainer -i \fIfile\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Convert a Compose file to Portainer-safe YAML (strips
.B build:
directives, warns on incompatibilities).
Output goes to stdout unless
.B -o
is specified.
.RS
.PP
python3 portainer-convert.py to-portainer -i docker-compose.yml
.br
python3 portainer-convert.py to-portainer -i docker-compose.yml -o portainer-stack.yml
.br
python3 portainer-convert.py to-portainer -i docker-compose.yml --stack-name myapp --deploy
.br
python3 portainer-convert.py to-portainer -i docker-compose.yml --stack-name myapp --deploy --update
.RE
.TP
.B from-portainer --stack-name \fIname\fR -o \fIfile\fR
Pull a stack from Portainer and save as a local Compose file.
.RS
.PP
python3 portainer-convert.py from-portainer --stack-name myapp -o docker-compose.yml
.RE
.SH HOMELAB COMPOSE FILES
.SS Quick start
Each service folder contains
.B docker-compose.yml
and
.BR install.sh .
Run install.sh — it checks prerequisites, creates config from examples, and starts the container.
If secrets are needed it will exit after creating the file; edit it, then re-run.
.PP
.RS
cd ~/dockersource/<service-name>
.br
bash install.sh
.RE
.SS Generic bootstrap
.B generic/
is a universal bootstrapper for any container that provides a
.B docker run
command (e.g. Twingate, Cloudflare, Tailscale):
.PP
1. Run
.BR "bash generic/install.sh"
.br
2. Enter a folder name — the script creates it and all files go there
.br
3. In a second SSH session,
.B cd
to that folder and run the provider's
.B docker run
command
.br
4. Press Enter — the script inspects the running container and generates
.B docker-compose.yml
+
.B .env
in that folder
.br
5. Review if needed, then confirm to start
.PP
Generated files are gitignored (they contain credentials).
.SS Container index
.TP
.B portainer/
portainer/portainer-ce — Container management UI. Ports: 9443, 9000.
.TP
.B busybox/
busybox — Utility shell with host filesystem access.
.TP
.B dozzle/
amir20/dozzle — Real-time container log viewer. Port: 8077.
.TP
.B netalertx/
ghcr.io/netalertx/netalertx — Network device monitoring and alerts. Port: 20211.
On Raspberry Pi requires
.B cap_add: [NET_ADMIN, NET_RAW]
and
.B security_opt: [seccomp:unconfined]
(already included in compose file).
.TP
.B netwatch/
Build from source — Home network monitor: device catalog, categories, power-on/off alarms. Port: 8095.
Requires
.BR config.yml :
set
.B scanner.network
(CIDR) and
.B scanner.interface
(e.g.
.IR eth0 ).
.TP
.B homarr/
ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr — Homelab dashboard. Port: 7575.
.B SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY
in
.B .env
is auto-generated by install.sh (openssl, /dev/urandom fallback) — no manual
step.
.B findtargetcontainers.sh
scans the local Docker node and mirrors the containers as app tiles on the
default board: new containers are added, removed containers disappear on the
next run, manually created tiles are never touched. Idempotent; supports
.BR --dry-run ,
.BR --all ,
.B --board
.IR name ,
and per-container docker labels
.BR homarr.ignore / homarr.url / homarr.icon .
Built-in special cases: background containers (twingate, cloudflared,
portainer agent) get no tile; calibre links to its https UI (:8092) plus an
extra content-server tile (:8081); netwatch links to :8095 (host network
mode, no published ports); marcujump gets an extra Handbuch tile
(/MarcuJumpGuide.html); FlashForgeAdventurer5MAPI links to
:9876/en/<printer-ip> (printer IP from the flashforge.printer_ip label set by
flashforge/install.sh). After each sync the board is compacted (gaps from
removed tiles closed, tiles repacked top-left). See homarr/README.md.
.TP
.B sudokusolver/
Build from source — AI-powered Sudoku solver web app. Port: 8011.
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
in
.B .env
is optional; enables image import.
.TP
.B marcujump/
Build from source — "Markus im Weltall" browser jump-and-run game served by
nginx. Port: 8093. The game is cloned from
.I https://github.com/refap3/marcujump
at build time, so the image always ships the current upstream version; the
Docker host needs internet access during build. Guide at
.IR /MarcuJumpGuide.html .
.B update.sh
compares the upstream index.html (SHA-256) with the copy inside the running
container and rebuilds only if the game changed.
.TP
.B flashforge/
Build from source — API + GUI to monitor a FlashForge Adventurer 5M (Pro)
3D printer, from
.IR https://github.com/IgorZyktin/FlashForgeAdventurer5MAPI .
Port: 9876. Container name: FlashForgeAdventurer5MAPI.
.B install.sh
asks for the printer IP (default 192.168.1.113;
.B PRINTER_IP
for non-interactive use), stores it in .env and as the
.B flashforge.printer_ip
container label, clones the upstream source and builds. GUI at
.IR http://<host>:9876/en/<printer-ip> ,
API at
.IR http://<host>:9876/api/execute/<printer-ip>/progress .
Re-run install.sh to change the IP or pull upstream updates.
.TP
.B watchtower/
containrrr/watchtower — On-demand container image updater. Runs once then exits; cleans up old images.
Trigger with:
.B docker start watchtower && docker logs -f watchtower
.TP
.B cloudflared/
cloudflare/cloudflared — Cloudflare Tunnel (zero-trust ingress). Requires
.B TUNNEL_TOKEN
in
.BR .env .
.TP
.B twingate-connector/
twingate/connector — Twingate zero-trust network connector. Requires
.BR TWINGATE_NETWORK ,
.BR TWINGATE_ACCESS_TOKEN ,
.B TWINGATE_REFRESH_TOKEN
in
.BR .env .
.TP
.B wg-easy/
ghcr.io/wg-easy/wg-easy — WireGuard VPN with web UI. Port: 51821.
.TP
.B filebrowser/
filebrowser/filebrowser — Web UI for browsing and managing files. Port: 8099.
Password is randomly generated on first start; retrieve with
.BR "docker logs filebrowser" ,
then change under Settings → User Management.
.TP
.B calibre/
lscr.io/linuxserver/calibre — Full Calibre desktop streamed to the browser via
KasmVNC. Ports: 8092 (desktop UI, HTTPS only — plain http is rejected by the
streaming stack; accept the self-signed certificate warning), 8081 (content
server for browsing, uploading, and downloading books; plain http works),
8091 (http, only usable behind a TLS reverse proxy).
.B install.sh
bootstraps the library, skips the welcome wizard, and enables the content
server with auto-start and no authentication; trusted_ips allows LAN clients
to upload and edit books without login (LAN-open read/write; do not
port-forward 8081).
Upload/download files via the KasmVNC side panel; convert books via the
desktop UI. Requires arm64 (Pi 4/5, 64-bit OS).
.SS Updating containers
.PP
.RS
cd ~/dockersource && git pull
.br
cd <service-name>
.br
docker compose up -d --build          # build-from-source (netwatch, sudokusolver, marcujump; flashforge: re-run install.sh)
.br
docker compose pull && docker compose up -d   # image-based (all others)
.RE
.PP
.BR netwatch ,
.BR sudokusolver ,
and
.B marcujump
also have
.B update.sh
that handles this in one step.
For
.B marcujump
no git pull of this repo is needed — its update.sh checks the upstream game
repo directly.
Config files (.env, config.yml) and data volumes are never touched by an update.
.SH SYNOLOGY VARIANTS
The
.B synology/
folder contains Synology NAS versions of the compose files.
Differences from Pi versions:
.IP \(bu 3
Named Docker volumes replaced with bind mounts to
.IR /volume1/docker/<app>/
.IP \(bu 3
.B filebrowser
mounts
.I /volume1
instead of
.I /
.IP \(bu 3
.B netalertx
uses Synology default PUID/PGID (1026/100) — verify with
.B id <username>
on your NAS
.SS Synology setup
.PP
.RS
sudo mkdir -p /volume1/docker/portainer /volume1/docker/netalertx \\
.br
  /volume1/docker/homarr /volume1/docker/wg-easy
.br
sudo mkdir -p /volume1/docker/filebrowser && sudo chmod 777 /volume1/docker/filebrowser
.RE
.PP
For
.BR homarr :
.PP
.RS
cd ~/dockersource/synology/homarr
.br
echo "SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" > .env
.RE
.SS wg-easy on Synology
WireGuard requires kernel module support. Verify before deploying:
.PP
.RS
modinfo wireguard
.RE
.PP
If this errors, wg-easy will not work on your NAS model.
.SS Synology container index
.TP
.B synology/portainer/
Same as portainer/ with bind mount for data.
.TP
.B synology/netalertx/
Same as netalertx/ with bind mount; check PUID/PGID.
.TP
.B synology/homarr/
Same as homarr/ with bind mount for appdata.
.TP
.B synology/wg-easy/
Same as wg-easy/ with bind mount; requires WireGuard kernel module.
.TP
.B synology/filebrowser/
Same as filebrowser/ but mounts /volume1 as root; uses port 8080 internally.
.PP
dozzle, watchtower, cloudflared, and twingate-connector have no Synology variant — standard compose files work as-is.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/dockersource/portainer-convert.py
Portainer stack sync CLI.
.TP
.I ~/.portainer-convert.json
Saved connection settings (URL, token, endpoint ID).
.TP
.I ~/dockersource/<service>/docker-compose.yml
Compose file for each container.
.TP
.I ~/dockersource/<service>/.env.example
Secret variable template; copy to
.B .env
and fill in before running.
.TP
.I ~/dockersource/<service>/install.sh
First-run installer for each container.
.TP
.I ~/dockersource/<service>/update.sh
One-step updater (netwatch and sudokusolver only).
